# Which languages have the most native speakers?
subtitle: "Rank five great languages by native speakers, then see how the order flips when you count everyone who speaks them."

## Which languages have the most native speakers?
text: {"font_size":36}
sources:
    - id: eth
      title: 'Ethnologue: Languages of the World (2025 and 2026 editions)'
      authors: Eberhard, Simons & Fennig (SIL)
      year: 2025
      finding: 'first-language speakers: Mandarin about 940-990 million, Spanish about 490 million, English about 370-390 million, Hindi about 345-350 million, French about 75 million; total speakers: English about 1.5 billion, Mandarin 1.2 billion, Hindi 610 million, Spanish 560 million, French 310 million'

    cards langs cites ["eth"] x 200 y 540 width 780 ends ["most","fewest"] hidden true
        * "Mandarin" icon.of "flag china" icon.set twemoji
        * "Spanish" icon.of "flag spain" icon.set twemoji
        * "English" icon.of "flag united kingdom" icon.set twemoji
        * "Hindi" icon.of "flag india" icon.set twemoji
        * "French" icon.of "flag france" icon.set twemoji
    text h_nat "native" #5e584e x 100 y 400 font_size 34 hidden true
    text h_tot "all speakers" #5e584e x 100 y 290 font_size 30 hidden true
    text n_zh "~1 bn" #2f6b8f cites ["eth"] x 278 y 400 font_size 36 hidden true
    text t_zh "1.2 bn" #5e584e cites ["eth"] x 278 y 290 font_size 36 hidden true
    text n_es "490 M" #2f6b8f cites ["eth"] x 434 y 400 font_size 36 hidden true
    text t_es "560 M" #5e584e cites ["eth"] x 434 y 290 font_size 36 hidden true
    text n_en "370 M" #2f6b8f cites ["eth"] x 590 y 400 font_size 36 hidden true
    text t_en "1.5 bn" #b5482e cites ["eth"] x 590 y 290 font_size 36 hidden true
    text n_hi "350 M" #2f6b8f cites ["eth"] x 746 y 400 font_size 36 hidden true
    text t_hi "610 M" #5e584e cites ["eth"] x 746 y 290 font_size 36 hidden true
    text n_fr "75 M" #2f6b8f cites ["eth"] x 902 y 400 font_size 36 hidden true
    text t_fr "310 M" #5e584e cites ["eth"] x 902 y 290 font_size 36 hidden true

    card title "Most native speakers?"

Five of the world's great languages. Which has the most native speakers, the people who learned it first, as children?
    draw langs

    ask "Put these languages in order of native speakers, from most to fewest. Drag the cards, then press Answer." on langs store r
        right: You got {r}.
        wrong: You got {r}.

Mandarin wins by a mile: nearly a billion people grew up speaking it.
    draw h_nat n_zh

Spanish comes second, thanks to Latin America, with almost half a billion.
    draw n_es

Then English and Hindi, close together at around three hundred and fifty million or so each.
    draw n_en n_hi

French, for all its fame, has only about seventy-five million native speakers.
    draw n_fr

But count everyone who speaks a language, natively or not, and the order changes.
    draw h_tot t_zh t_es t_en t_hi t_fr

English jumps to first, with about one and a half billion speakers. Most of them learned it as a second language.
    text first "1st" #b5482e x 590 y 220 font_size 40

So the world's most spoken language is mostly spoken with an accent.
    highlight t_en effect circle

